Title = {Physics-informed neural network-based model predictive control for
   chiller plant - fan coil unit system and intelligent human-AI
   interaction via large language model},
Journal = {ENERGY},
Year = {2025},
Volume = {339},
Month = {DEC 1},
Abstract = {The advanced building control technology, like model predictive control
   (MPC), can achieve significant energy savings and mitigate greenhouse
   gas emissions for heating, ventilation, and air conditioning (HVAC)
   system. In this study, we propose a novel MPC controller for chiller
   plant-fan coil unit system. The overall method includes three folds.
   First, a physics-informed neural network (PINN) is proposed to predict
   the dynamic of chilled water return temperature. Combing data and
   physics knowledge, the proposed PINN model has good generalization
   performance and it can capture the dynamic of chilled water temperature
   through black-box module and physics module. Second, the developed PINN
   model is employed in an MPC controller as its system dynamic model
   (state-space model). And the overall optimization problem is formulated
   as a mixed-integer linear programming (MILP) to minimize system total
   power and user discomfort. Third, an AI agent is developed based on
   large language model (LLM) to automatically tune the parameters of MPC
   controller based on operator's feedback. The system operators don't need
   to know about any piece of MPC controller, while the AI agent can
   understand the content of MPC controller and interact with operators.
   Comprehensive experiments are conducted to validate the proposed method
   using real-world data. The results showed that the PINN outperformed
   pure black-box model for a large margin. And the ideal MPC controller
   achieved 8.4 \% energy savings comparing with rule-based control. The AI
   agent correctly tuned the MPC parameters in five scenarios, and the
   average cost was only},
